WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:02.302
After weeks of relentless fighting,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.671
Ukraine says Russian troops are advancing

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.206
on the city of Bakhmut.

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.440
Now, according to Ukrainian

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.475
military officials,

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.309
Russian forces

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.243
are assaulting

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.946
the city itself, suggesting that

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.180
it is no longer

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.750
simply operating on the outskirts.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:20.053
But Ukraine does not plan to withdraw yet

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.088
its defense forces are still holding on

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.056
to their positions

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.291
and are repelling Russian attacks.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.961
Now, the boss of the mystery Wagner

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.162
Group says this video you're

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.397
looking at here

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.865
shows is fighters practically

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.933
in the center of the city.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.836
However, CNN has geolocated this video

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.039
to be the east of Bakhmut,

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.173
around two kilometers or

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.308
so from the city center.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.310
Meanwhile, Ukraine fears

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.412
that if Paramount falls

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.679
the town of Charles River,

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:47.280
as you can see,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.350
there will be the next on Russia's list.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.951
Alex Marquardt is there

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.221
This is the road

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.923
on the way to back mud

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.225
cars, military vehicles

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.861
bombing up and down this road, going to

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.597
and from the front

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:08.435
You see this armored vehicle right here

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:12.205
as a sign for victory.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.374
There are still some people here,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.208
not too many,

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.444
but some of these hardy residents

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:18.311
have stayed behind.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.647
This is the shop of Sea views.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.748
Who is here?

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.716
Grilling meats held shashlik.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.919
He actually fled from Bark Mound

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.120
two months ago

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.856
and has opened up the shop selling basics

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.492
like bananas, beetroot and and candles.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.626
There's another man

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.661
who here who we just met

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:37.130
whose daughter is still in mud.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.466
One of the thousands of people there

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.202
who have been asked to evacuate

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.770
but are still in the city.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.572
Amid this incredible fighting,

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.406
you can see that

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.374
they put up wood there, too,

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.909
to protect those windows.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:53.012
So much destruction in this town.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.914
We were just farther in

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.182
the center of town, is called it,

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:56.850
because if you are,

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.051
this is one town

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.719
over from back

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.287
with a large group of people

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.222
at a bus stop

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.290
waiting for a water delivery

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.126
that never came.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.594
Every few moments

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.596
you can hear explosions.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:10.730
The sound of

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:11.364
what we believe

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.433
to be outgoing artillery fire.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.803
Ukrainians firing at Russian positions.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.638
We spoke with an older

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.473
woman named Valentina

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:20.974
who said that

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.810
there is so much flying over their heads

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.012
that she is scared all the time.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.747
That they are so close

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.082
to the Russian positions.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.152
That's more outgoing artillery fire.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:32.886
They are so close

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.487
to the Russian positions

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.122
that they can walk there.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.524
We also spoke

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.791
with some Ukrainian soldiers

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.759
like these ones

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.395
who man one of those artillery positions.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.565
They told us that there has been no order

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.700
to pull back from back mount,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.501
that there are fighting

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.303
because if they give up back mud,

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.938
then this town transfer,

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.473
this would be next.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.441
And that is what everyone is thinking

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.177
now, that if

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.480
Russia were to take back mud,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.549
that they would have another foothold

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.150
in this region

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.651
from which

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.486
to try to push farther

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.588
into eastern Ukraine.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.958
Alex Marquardt, CNN, in charge of air.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.992
Well, for the first time

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.694
since Russia invaded Ukraine, U.S.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:15.461
Secretary of State

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:16.696
Antony Blinken has met

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.830
with Russian Foreign Minister

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:18.932
Sergei Lavrov.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.366
They spoke for about 10 minutes

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.234
on the sidelines

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.835
of the G20 foreign ministers meeting.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.437
That's happening in New Delhi.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.872
Discussing the war in Ukraine,

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:26.739
the new START

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.575
nuclear arms reduction treaty

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.209
and Pull Will

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:29.976
and of course, the US

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.211
citizen who's been in Russian

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.879
prison system for years.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.547
Natasha Bertrand is following the story

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.915
and joins me now from Washington.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.684
So Natasha, what more do we know

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.118
came out of that meeting

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.820
and indeed who initiated this meeting

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.521
to start off with?

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:43.323
Yeah.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:43.890
So we're actually

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.324
told that

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.558
it was the Secretary of State,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.259
Antony Blinken,

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.827
who did initiate that meeting

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.661
and you know,

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.495
it was described

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.198
more as a spur of the moment type thing

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.500
where Blinken did seek out Lavrov

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.502
on the sidelines of the G20

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.670
to have a conversation

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.972
with him about various subjects.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.073
But there were no formal

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.174
negotiations, right?

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.342
Nothing very

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.576
formal in terms of a meeting

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:04.611
between the US and Russia.

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.612
But it was an opportunity

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.013
for Blinken to raise

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.481
a couple of very key issues.

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.349
Among them, of course,

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.783
the New START treaty,

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.051
trying to encourage the Russians

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:15.088
to get back into that nuclear arms treaty

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.556
that they withdrew from

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.323
just a couple of weeks

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.424
ago, saying that responsible

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.559
nations need,

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.160
of course, these nuclear guardrails.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:21.828
And then, of course,

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:24.063
he brought up the case of Paul Whelan,

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.231
who is the American

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.066
who has been detained in Russia

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.668
for nearly five years.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:30.036
Of course,
the US now

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.204
says that they have put forward

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.639
another substantive proposal

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:34.540
to Russia to get Paul Whelan back,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.776
but that the Russians have not engaged.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:37.877
And then finally, of course,

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.079
the biggest subject of all is that

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.114
is the war in Ukraine.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.448
And he encouraged the Russians,

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.783
of course, to abide

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:44.984
or to to sit down

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:45.985
and talk with the Ukrainians

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.220
and come to a peace agreement,

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.388
noting that the Ukrainians,

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.289
President Olinsky,

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.890
had put forward a ten point peace

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.258
plan of his own

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.960
and for the Russians to start engaging

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.061
with that in good faith.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.095
And that was really the overall

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.664
theme of the discussions,

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.531
Blinken said at

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.734
the G-20 was not only urging Russia

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.069
to pull out of Ukraine,

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.605
but also warning other allies of China's

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.740
potential plans to arm

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.241
Russia

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.076
with lethal equipment, saying that

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:12.545
that is just unacceptable to the US

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:13.413
and that many allies

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:14.347
are concerned about that.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.615
So it was an opportunity

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.517
for Blinken rather informally

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.319
to meet face to face with Lavrov

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:21.421
for the first time since the war began.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.923
And raised these top issues of concern

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.458
for the United States. These.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.894
And sticking with Ukraine

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:30.663
were G20 leaders on the same page

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:32.598
in regard to the war in Ukraine, because

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.866
there was no communique

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:36.402
Not exactly.

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.905
So according to the Russian readout

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.773
of their meeting with the Chinese,

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:41.407
they say that

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:42.675
the Russians and the Chinese

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.577
were very much on the same page

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:46.012
with regard to the war in Ukraine.

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:46.346
Of course,

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:48.214
China did issue its own

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:48.781
kind of peace

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.283
proposal for that war

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.050
that the United States

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.586
and the West are extremely skeptical of.

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:55.188
And the US has said.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.823
Anthony
Blinken said during a press conference

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:57.457
earlier today

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:59.492
that in fact the US had warned

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:02.028
many of the allies at that G-20 summit

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.529
about China's

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.898
contemplation of sending Russia

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:06.933
that lethal equipment

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:09.035
and the fact that many of those allies

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.303
were deeply concerned by that.

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:10.903
And so

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:11.304
I think

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.005
what you saw here was kind of a divide,

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:13.373
of course,

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:15.074
between the kind of us led

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:15.942
Western alliance

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:16.676
at the G20,

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:18.945
the kind of China Russia alliance there,

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:20.646
and then India, which was of course

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:21.647
the host of the summit,

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:22.482
kind of in the middle.

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:23.616
Of course, we have seen the U.S.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:24.984
express concerns

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:25.852
about India

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:27.253
not condemning

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.287
Russia's war in Ukraine,

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:29.822
and of course, India buying up

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:30.690
a lot of that oil

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.692
that is keeping Russian profits afloat

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.160
and allowing them to continue the war.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.495
So it was a really interesting

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:36.229
dynamic here.

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.397
But of course, we're seeing the push

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:39.599
and pull on both sides from the US

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:41.134
and from Russia, China, India,

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:42.835
to basically come

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.971
to some kind of solution here

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:45.471
with regard to

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:45.838
the war

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:47.073
does not look like

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:47.640
that's going to happen

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.242
any time soon, however.

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:49.609
Yeah.

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.210
Natasha Bertrand for us in Washington,

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.612
thanks very much, Natasha.

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:53.312
So let's discuss

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:54.547
all of this with retired

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:56.315
Air Force Colonel Cedric Leighton

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.550
and CNN political

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.418
and national security

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:00.286
analyst David Sanger.

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:01.654
David, I want to start with you.

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:03.689
So a State Department official told us

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.558
not to expect Russia

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:07.293
to change course after this meeting.

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.362
That's not particularly surprising.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.563
But the source also said

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.098
that Blinken was the one

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:13.499
who approached Lavrov

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:15.802
on the sidelines of the G-20 here.

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:18.271
Why does the US want to have

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:19.472
this kind of engagement

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.573
with Russia at this moment?

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:23.409
Well, Abby,

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:23.976
there's been

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:27.380
very little conversation at high levels

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.782
between Russia and the United States

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:30.850
in the year

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:31.951
plus a few days

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.953
since the invasion happened.

00:07:33.953 --> 00:07:35.154
It was only one phone

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:38.124
call on the question of prisoner releases

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:41.961
between Secretary Blinken and Lavrov.

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:45.031
The last time they had met in person,

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:47.066
Blinken confronted

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:48.401
Lavrov with the evidence

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:50.403
that an invasion was about to happen.

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.905
And Lavrov continued to denial that

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:55.408
that Russia was going to invade.

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:55.942
And in fact,

00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:57.677
we believe that Lavrov probably

00:07:57.677 --> 00:07:59.946
wasn't told about the invasion

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:02.882
until just hours before it happened.

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:04.016
So there's a

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.251
really interesting question here

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:06.552
about whether he's the right person

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:08.221
to be talking to.

00:08:08.254 --> 00:08:09.155
But since you

00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:10.623
can't have President Biden

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.825
talking to Putin, these days,

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.161
this is the only real channel left.

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:16.729
I think the most important part of that,

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:18.197
obviously trying to get Paul Way

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:18.998
Whalen out,

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.300
but also communicating directly

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.269
with the Russians about the long term

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:26.806
danger of their suspension of involvement

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:28.774
in the New START treaty,

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:30.376
because that treaty expires

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.078
in three years.

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:33.813
And there's almost no chance

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:35.781
that there's going to be a negotiation

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:37.483
to extend it, at which point

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:39.318
there will be no limits on either

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:41.020
country's nuclear forces.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:41.521
Yeah,

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:43.322
I mean, Colonel Leighton, on that point,

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:46.592
what is the strategic value for Russia

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:49.128
in suspending their participation

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:50.162
in this treaty?

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:50.630
Are they now

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:51.831
free to engage

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:53.132
in expanding their arsenal?

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:54.600
And is there any putting the genie

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.502
back in the bottle if that happens?

00:08:58.437 --> 00:08:59.839
Yeah, that's a big problem, Abby.

00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:01.807
And I'm actually very concerned

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:03.142
that the genie might not be able

00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:03.476
to be

00:09:03.476 --> 00:09:05.912
put back in the bottle at this point.

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:08.748
As to what the Russians want to do is

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:09.415
they could

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:12.018
potentially be able to use

00:09:12.418 --> 00:09:13.953
this lack of limits.

00:09:13.953 --> 00:09:14.854
They have a little less

00:09:14.854 --> 00:09:16.622
than 6000 warheads

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:18.457
right now in their nuclear arsenal.

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:20.493
They could potentially expand that number

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:22.528
and they could also develop

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:23.296
newer weapons.

00:09:23.296 --> 00:09:24.997
We talked to before

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:26.332
about their hypersonic

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:28.034
weapons capability.

00:09:28.034 --> 00:09:30.202
We also know that they may be refining

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:31.971
some of their nuclear capabilities.

00:09:31.971 --> 00:09:33.139
So that's the kind of thing

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:33.806
that we're looking at.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:35.474
It would not surprise me

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:37.443
if they would want to try to modernize

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:39.545
their nuclear forces during this period.

00:09:39.946 --> 00:09:40.780
And so that is something

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:41.781
that we would definitely have to

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:42.548
watch out for.

